 26. **`ImportRunOptions` stays a separate object, and is OPEN** (round 8). It is kept apart from `ImportRunContext` because it is exactly ONE persisted column (`ps_import_run.options` JSON) with its own serialization boundary (`fromArray()`/`toArray()`) — the adapter reads and writes that column without touching anything else — whereas the context is the whole runtime state, mixing frozen config with the progress that moves as batches run. Merging them would put 5+N option accessors on a class that already carries the phase, offset, cursor and skipped rows. The typed properties are only the options the CORE engine knows (today `forceIds` and `matchRef` are the only two PR1 actually reads; `truncate`/`sendEmail`/`dryRun` are the PR2 sequencer's), but **the set is not closed**: any other key travels in an `$extra` bag, round-trips untouched through `toArray()`, and is readable via `get()`/`has()`/`getExtra()`. That retention is the point, not a nicety — the context is rebuilt from the database on EVERY batch request, so an unknown key that `fromArray()` dropped (as it used to) would silently vanish between two batches, making importer-specific options impossible for module importers. Pinned by `ImportRunOptionsTest`.
 
